# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Candidate data and screening output — NEVER commit these.
# A public repository containing real CVs, phone numbers or a blacklist is a
# personal-data leak (and, in most jurisdictions, a reportable one).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2_Active_CVs/
TOP_CV/
TOP_CV_*/
OLD_TOP_CV*/
Evaluation_Output/
3_Evaluation_Output/
blacklist.csv

# The client's own posting. It names the client, the salary and the location —
# it is their material, not yours to publish. The app never falls back to a
# committed JD: the recruiter uploads one (UI) or drops it here.
1_Active_JD/

# Raw posting files (PDF/DOCX) that land in data/ — real postings, never commit.
data/*.pdf
data/*.docx
data/*.doc
# The committed data/ fixtures are the synthetic .txt/.csv demo pair only.
data/*.xlsx
data/*.xls

# Root-level scratch dumps: per-candidate debug notes that contain real names
# and phone numbers. `requirements.txt` is the one root .txt that is the
# project, so it is explicitly kept.
/*.txt
!/requirements.txt

# Verification fixtures are built from real CV text.
.verify/

# ── Local environment / scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
.freebuff/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
*.tmp

# Archived pre-scrub git history created by scripts/publish-github.sh —
# it contains the pre-cleanup snapshot, so it must never be committed.
.git-pre-scrub-backup*/

# ── Web app ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
# Local wrangler/miniflare state: sqlite caches, built bundles and source maps
# produced by `wrangler dev`. Build output, not source.
web/.wrangler/
.wrangler/
